improves on the “optimised Strassen bound” (1.1) by a superpolyno mial factor, i.e.,
by an arbitrarily large power of log N . Hittmeir’s algorithm relies on an trick that
seems to have ﬁrst been suggested by Pollard [Pol78, §3]: if N is a semiprime pq,
then Euler’s theorem implies that
αp+q ≡ αN +1 (mod N ) (1.3)
