deduce (a − d)− 1,... , (a + d)− 1; this is done is a single sweep of T2, and the results
are stored on a tape T3. Then, using Lemma 4, all δ(i, d)− 1 are computed and stored
on a tape T4, and all Δ( a, i, d)o nat a p e T5. The whole cost up to now is O(dmR),
the cost of the tape movements being O(dℓ). The space complexity is in O(dℓ + sR).
The coeﬃcients of S are copied from T3 to a tape T6, and those of ˜P are computed
and stored on a tape T7; the cost is O(dmR), since the data are well organized on
tapes. We then compute the product of S and ˜P. The result is the list of coeﬃcients
Qk, stored on a tape T8 after a time 2 MR(d)+ O(dmR). Finally the target values
